  "note": "Round 51, for Wheat on the image-free kit with the standalone Python: edits of community fine-tunes, of Mistral pretrained bases and of two Google checkpoints, each measured against the parent its card names: grayarea/Magidonia-24B-v4.3-heretic-v1.2, nchapman/Ministral-3-14B-Instruct-2512-heretic-BF16, grayarea/Skyfall-31B-v4.1-Heretic-v1.2, darkc0de/Mistral-Small-3.2-24B-Instruct-2506-heretic, keithtyser/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-local-abliterated-sota-internal-t34, AlSamCur123/gemma-4-E4B-it-uncensored-continued, nchapman/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-heretic-BF16, OS-Software/CyberStag-Security-26B-A4B-V1-Uncensored-Heretic. nchapman's two Ministral 3 copies name the instruct checkpoints in their cards and the pretrained bases in their fields, so they are pinned against the bases and the read-out says what that shows; OS-Software's copy names the pretrained 26B-A4B. Left out on the way: grayarea's Magistral Small pass, measured in round 18; darkc0de's Mistral Small 4 119B, whose original is float8 on the hub; yamatazen's Shisa v2 and Himeyuri Magnum merges, whose chains hold a base the lineage cannot place; DavidAU's 1B pass, whose name carries a restricted maker's model name and fails the gate; and Jiunsong's 26B, whose declared parent is not a repository the hub serves. No measured pair is repeated and no copy duplicates a measured weight file by checksum."
